WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.264
Another three centimeters
to the right

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.964
and you would have severed
your brachial artery.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.097
Autosuture, please.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.197
And if that had happened,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.231
you would have bled to death
right there in the holosuite.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.641
The human fascination
with "what might have been"

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.873
is tiresome, Doctor.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.074
The artery is not severed
and I am not dead.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.981
Oh, well, forgive me
for boring you.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.313
Let me get straight
to the point.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.580
You're acting like a fool.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.952
Your observation is noted.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.651
But spending two years
in a Dominion prison camp

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.216
has dulled my reflexes.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.387
This only proves that
I need further training.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.624
Turning off the holosuite
safety protocols

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.258
during a battle simulation
is, at best, dubious.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.734
For a man with only one eye,
it's positively idiotic.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.466
Now, if you would consider
ocular replacement...

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:42.441
I do not want
an artificial eye!

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:45.137
Then you must accept the fact
that you have a disability

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.270
and stop acting like...

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:51.648
There are limits as to how far
I will indulge you, Doctor.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.486
General Martok, there is

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.115
a priority message for you
from the Klingon High Council.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.257
We're done here.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.888
Route the message
to my quarters.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.056
Acknowledged.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.589
Doctor... thank you.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.067
If you really
want to thank me

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.967
don't walk in here
dripping blood anymore.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.062
It takes days to get it
out of the carpet.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.119
Check it now.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.884
Still no increase in phaser
relay efficiency, sir.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.156
The through-put reading
is steady at 148.7.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:38.562
Have you initialized
the interface program?

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.725
Yes, and then I charged
the prefire chamber

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.530
and recalibrated
the emitter stage.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.662
This thing just doesn't work!

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.728
Sir.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.001
Very well.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.633
We'll start over.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.974
Go to the Engine Room

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.478
and download
the operating system

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.810
into the computer core

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:57.476
but, this time,
do it one file at a time.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.110
Aye, sir.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.381
Good evening, General.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.517
Cadet.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.890
General.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.692
I did not expect you
until 2200 hours.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.927
I must cancel our appointment.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.697
I've received new orders
from the High Council...

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.465
a mission of some importance.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:19.597
I must prepare.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.765
Of course.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.298
May glory and honor
follow you on your journey.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.403
Ah... excuse me, sirs?

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.540
Could I just slip by?

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.990
How is the shoulder?

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:41.754
Oh, Dr. Bashir made
the necessary repairs.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.728
I told him it was
a holosuite accident.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.663
He would not understand
the need to draw blood

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.189
in a warrior's
training exercise.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.599
Few humans would.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:53.868
However, I do apologize again
for the inconvenience.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.772
I did not intend
to cause so much damage.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.300
I was the one who did not
parry the blow in time.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.575
A simple, foolish mistake

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.514
one that I would not have made
two years ago.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.643
Can you discuss the mission?

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:11.751
Three days ago,
the Battle Cruiser B'Moth

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.954
began a patrol
along the Cardassian border.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.464
They have not been
heard from since.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.693
They are now reported
as missing.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:24.066
It is possible she was
destroyed by the Dominion.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.697
The Jem'Hadar attacked
a Federation starship

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.331
near the border
less than a week ago.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:31.400
That is our assumption
as well, but we must be sure.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.275
So I have been given command

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:36.510
of a bird-of-prey...
the Rotarran...

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.346
to conduct a search
for the B'Moth.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.874
This is the first time

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:43.685
I will have led troops
in the field since...

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.715
my confinement by the Dominion.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.989
It must be an exciting prospect.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.963
I tell you, Worf...
without shame...

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.728
there were days
in that prison camp

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.292
when the thought that
I would never again

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:02.570
set foot in a Klingon vessel
made me weep like an old woman.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.510
I envy you the days ahead.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.513
It will be a glorious adventure.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:12.246
An adventure that we
could share, my friend.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.254
I need someone I can
trust at my side

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.848
someone whose loyalty
I can count on.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.790
Worf, son of Mogh

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.956
I ask you to join me
on this mission

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.795
as my friend...

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.825
and as my First Officer.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:36.060
I've told the General
that I'm inclined

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:39.292
to grant his request
for your services, Commander.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:42.324
I can certainly understand
why he wants you along.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.892
You're a fine officer.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.096
But I'm not sure

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:47.197
why you want to go
on this mission.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.468
It is a great honor

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.976
to be asked to serve
under General Martok.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.276
And he saved my life
in the Dominion prison camp.

00:06:55.315 --> 00:06:57.749
Oh? You didn't put that
in your mission report.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.809
It was a personal matter.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:02.150
Not something that belongs
in an official report.

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.780
Go on.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.814
You know that I was
forced to fight

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.792
the Jem'Hadar guards
in the camp.

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:09.761
Each day they would
call me to the ring

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.457
and each day I would fight

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:16.457
but then there came a day
when I... wavered.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:19.300
You mean you didn't want
to go back into the ring?

00:07:19.339 --> 00:07:22.399
No. I mean I considered
letting them kill me.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:24.706
It seemed like the only way out.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:26.302
Just before I went into the ring

00:07:26.346 --> 00:07:28.473
Martok turned to wish me success

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.141
and then he saw
what I was planning...

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.117
he saw it in my eyes.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.483
It was a moment of tova'dok.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.817
Of what?

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.551
There is no human word for it.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:41.856
It is a moment of... clarity

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.260
between two warriors
on a field of battle.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:46.288
Much is said
without the need for words.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:49.699
In that moment,
he knew what was in my mind.

00:07:49.736 --> 00:07:52.728
Once I realized that he saw
my intention to give up

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.967
I could no longer
go through with it.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.976
I went back into the ring
and fought once more.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:01.581
He had given me
his warrior's heart.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.610
Perhaps it is something
a human cannot understand.

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:15.025
As of this moment

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:17.427
you are relieved
of all Starfleet obligations

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.454
and placed on detached service

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:21.932
to the lmperial Klingon
Defense Forces.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.731
Thank you, sir.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.262
Mr. Worf.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:32.376
Qapla'!

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.112
Qapla'!

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.100
The revised duty roster.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.898
Read it and weep.

00:08:57.937 --> 00:09:00.667
Small arms recalibration?

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:02.401
Does that mean all
the small arms on the station?

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:03.408
Afraid so.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.070
And I need an experienced
combat officer to do it.

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:07.511
Worf has already set up
the parameters.

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:09.309
All you need to do
is just make sure it gets done.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.782
I'm the new
Intelligence Officer?

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:15.086
It has to be a Starfleet officer

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.679
with a level-4
security clearance.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.087
That means either you or Dax

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:21.059
and I need Dax to take over
as Fleet Liaison Officer.

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.355
Beats retuning phaser rifles.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:25.159
Well, I certainly hope
Worf's enjoying himself

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:28.030
while we're stuck here
taking over his duties.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.831
Julian, have you ever been
on a Klingon ship?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.304
If you think the Defiant
is cramped and uncomfortable

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:35.603
try spending a week
on a bird-of-prey.

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:38.109
Worf isn't exactly
taking a luxury cruise.

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:39.475
Serving on a Klingon ship

00:09:39.512 --> 00:09:41.810
is like being with a gang
of ancient sea pirates.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.748
You advance in rank by
killing the people above you.

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:45.842
So everywhere you turn

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:47.614
you're surrounded
by potential assassins.

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:48.620
Well, that's crazy.

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:49.848
How can a ship
function like that?

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:51.754
It's not quite that chaotic.

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:54.282
The social and military
hierarchy of a Klingon vessel

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:55.953
is very strictly enforced.

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:59.725
A subordinate can only
challenge a direct superior

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:00.959
and only under
certain conditions.

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:03.399
What sort of "conditions"?

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:05.427
Dereliction of duty

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:08.634
dishonorable conduct,
cowardice...

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.972
Cowardice? A Klingon?

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.305
It's been known to happen.

00:10:12.344 --> 00:10:14.744
The Klingons are
as diverse a people as any.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.975
Some of them are strong,
and some of them are weak.

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:18.881
I'd say those two

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:22.217
definitely fall
into the strong category.

00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:37.826
Trouble?

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:38.962
Not yet.

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:40.767
I can see why they
caught your attention.

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:42.103
Are they off Martok's new ship?

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:44.006
Just docked.

00:10:44.076 --> 00:10:45.668
They seem quiet enough.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:48.111
For the moment, maybe

00:10:48.147 --> 00:10:50.707
but you see the one on the left
wearing the necklace?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.274
Yes.

00:10:52.318 --> 00:10:53.785
Those are neck bones...

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:55.377
Cardassian neck bones.

00:11:01.861 --> 00:11:04.193
Decided not to wear
the sash after all?

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.755
Officially, there is no
House of Mogh in the Empire

00:11:06.799 --> 00:11:07.788
so I saw little point

00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:09.801
in wearing its emblem
on a Klingon ship.

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.803
How do you think
the crew's going to feel

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:13.896
about serving under a man
without a House?

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:16.100
How they feel is unimportant.

00:11:16.142 --> 00:11:19.236
All I require from them
is obedience.

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.838
Spoken like an uncaring,
hard-nosed autocrat...

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:23.781
the quintessential
First Officer.

00:11:25.684 --> 00:11:28.653
I-I do not wish
to have a lengthy good-bye.

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:31.713
I wasn't planning
on having one.

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.088
Good.

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:45.998
Jadzia.

00:11:46.071 --> 00:11:47.629
Yes.

00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:49.004
I think it would be better

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.975
to part company
here on the station.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.500
Oh, I'm coming with you.

00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:53.910
What?

00:11:53.946 --> 00:11:55.937
The Rotarran is shorthanded

00:11:55.981 --> 00:11:58.347
and I still have
four months leave coming.

00:11:58.384 --> 00:12:00.978
And I've already cleared it
with Martok and Benjamin.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.578
I'm your new Science Officer.

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:04.748
Why did you not tell me?

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.519
It's more fun this way.

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:08.254
And after getting a good look

00:12:08.294 --> 00:12:10.922
at a couple members
of the Rotarran's crew

00:12:10.963 --> 00:12:14.160
I don't think we're going
to be having a lot of fun

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.997
on this mission.

00:12:37.056 --> 00:12:38.023
Boo!

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:46.924
Ros-te-ka cha'Domak
ootha Trill?

00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:49.196
I am Tavana,
Engineering Officer.

00:12:49.235 --> 00:12:51.567
I'm Jadzia Dax, Science Officer.

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:52.969
Dax?

00:12:53.005 --> 00:12:55.132
Are you related
to the great Curzon Dax?

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:57.540
Curzon was the last host
for my symbiont.

00:12:57.576 --> 00:12:58.804
I carry his memories.

00:12:58.844 --> 00:12:59.811
Ah!

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:04.680
My mother met the great Curzon
on the Homeworld once.

00:13:04.717 --> 00:13:06.878
She said he was
very taken with her.

00:13:06.919 --> 00:13:11.151
Curzon was very "taken"
with many people.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.055
So was my mother.

00:13:26.071 --> 00:13:28.403
I am Worf, son of Mogh.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:33.207
I now take my place
as First Officer.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:36.840
I serve the Captain,
but I stand for the crew.

00:13:38.217 --> 00:13:41.550
Who brings the record of battle
for this ship?

00:13:52.498 --> 00:13:54.728
I, Kornan, son of Shovak

00:13:54.767 --> 00:13:56.598
Weapon's Officer
of the ship of Rotarran

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:58.364
present the glorious record
of our honor

00:13:58.404 --> 00:14:00.872
and hope that you may find us
worthy of your leadership.

00:14:07.546 --> 00:14:09.741
If you're looking for victories,
you won't find any.

00:14:09.782 --> 00:14:12.250
Not for the last seven months.

00:14:12.284 --> 00:14:16.653
I do not need help recognizing
a list of failures.

00:14:20.059 --> 00:14:21.924
It is clear to me

00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:25.897
that none of you are worthy
of my blood or my life.

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.791
But I will stand for you

00:14:29.835 --> 00:14:32.929
and together, we will restore
honor to this ship

00:14:32.972 --> 00:14:35.406
and bring glory to the Empire.

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:47.217
Ah...

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:54.685
I have accepted
the crew's battle records

00:14:54.727 --> 00:14:57.525
and on their behalf,
I pledge you our lives

00:14:57.563 --> 00:15:00.862
and ask that you lead us
as Commander of this ship.

00:15:05.604 --> 00:15:10.098
I accept your lives
into my hands.

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:11.734
De-lak DoH!

00:15:12.778 --> 00:15:14.837
Clear all moorings.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:16.142
Release docking clamps.

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.046
Docking clamps released.

00:15:18.083 --> 00:15:20.051
Bow thrusters ahead
one half.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.713
We have cleared
the docking ring.

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:26.725
Ahead one-quarter impulse.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.264
Helmsman, plot a direct course

00:15:33.298 --> 00:15:36.096
to the last known position
of the B'Moth, maximum warp.

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:38.968
No. That would take us
through the Tong Beak Nebula.

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:40.767
I want to go around the nebula.

00:15:40.806 --> 00:15:43.775
General, that will add
a full day to our journey.

00:15:43.809 --> 00:15:45.276
I'm aware of that.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.073
There are reports
of the Dominion

00:15:47.112 --> 00:15:48.739
operating ships in the nebula.

00:15:48.781 --> 00:15:51.375
I would like to avoid
a fight with the Jem'Hadar.

00:15:52.684 --> 00:15:55.346
You wish to... avoid a fight?

00:15:56.355 --> 00:16:00.451
Your tone does not sit well
with me, Helmsman.

00:16:01.727 --> 00:16:04.287
Our mission
is to find the B'Moth

00:16:04.329 --> 00:16:07.164
not to satisfy
your warrior's pride.

00:16:07.297 --> 00:16:09.060
My apologies, sir.

00:16:09.099 --> 00:16:11.397
I meant no disrespect.

00:16:11.434 --> 00:16:13.732
Then follow your orders
and lay in a course.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.032
Maximum warp.

00:16:15.071 --> 00:16:16.629
Yes, Commander.

00:16:16.673 --> 00:16:20.165
Maximum warp, around...

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:22.110
the nebula.

00:16:24.147 --> 00:16:25.876
Helm ready.

00:16:29.085 --> 00:16:30.712
Mahk-cha.

00:16:42.032 --> 00:16:45.593
Kol KeH less pooK loaD

00:16:45.635 --> 00:16:48.900
Kol pooK beH poo

00:16:48.939 --> 00:16:52.397
Yoch bow math bow je
Shuv weee

00:16:52.442 --> 00:16:55.775
Say moach chu may ew

00:16:55.812 --> 00:16:58.975
mah Shoov, maH nong,
ej ma choch chew

00:16:59.082 --> 00:17:02.415
nee beH yln maHj
ach wov, coo!

00:17:02.452 --> 00:17:04.750
Bath ma cheth bejj,
ej yo'

00:17:04.788 --> 00:17:06.619
Keej DaHk,
vav poo ma Dee muv

00:17:06.656 --> 00:17:08.453
pa-rech ma Shoov tach Koo

00:17:08.491 --> 00:17:13.428
ma mev Ko'ma Shoov
tach ma ov...

00:17:13.463 --> 00:17:16.626
Kol KeH less...

00:17:38.521 --> 00:17:39.954
Maybe you didn't read

00:17:40.056 --> 00:17:43.457
the crew roster,
but my name is Dax

00:17:43.493 --> 00:17:45.961
and I'm the new Science Officer
on this garbage scow

00:17:46.062 --> 00:17:48.929
and you were in my seat.

00:17:50.867 --> 00:17:53.335
I'm glad we understand
each other.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:55.838
Now get... down
to the other end

00:17:55.872 --> 00:17:57.362
where you belong.

00:18:02.479 --> 00:18:04.413
Stewed bok-rat liver?

00:18:04.447 --> 00:18:06.506
It's not very fresh.

00:18:06.549 --> 00:18:10.610
With a little bloodwine,
it might be acceptable.

00:18:10.654 --> 00:18:14.750
Ha. There's been no bloodwine
on this ship for six months.

00:18:14.791 --> 00:18:16.122
Really?

00:18:16.159 --> 00:18:18.719
Then I'm glad
I brought three barrels aboard

00:18:18.762 --> 00:18:20.923
before we left Deep Space 9.

00:18:22.165 --> 00:18:24.565
Three barrels?

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.601
"Dishonorable conduct.

00:18:28.638 --> 00:18:30.265
"Dereliction of duty.

00:18:30.307 --> 00:18:31.899
"Inattention to orders.

00:18:31.941 --> 00:18:33.374
"Unmotivated.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.571
Insufficiently aggressive."

00:18:35.612 --> 00:18:39.639
These personnel reports
read like prison records.

00:18:39.683 --> 00:18:40.672
We should remember

00:18:40.717 --> 00:18:42.378
that the Rotarran
has been defeated

00:18:42.419 --> 00:18:43.943
again and again
by the Jem'Hadar.

00:18:44.054 --> 00:18:46.955
It is not surprising
the crew morale has suffered.

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:49.925
It's more than a case
of low morale, Worf.

00:18:49.959 --> 00:18:52.723
This crew has been defeated
so many times

00:18:52.762 --> 00:18:57.290
they expect defeat,
and that is dangerous.

00:18:57.334 --> 00:18:59.461
They need a victory.

00:18:59.502 --> 00:19:01.527
One decisive battle
against the Jem'Hadar

00:19:01.571 --> 00:19:03.402
would do much
to lift their spirits.

00:19:04.774 --> 00:19:06.264
And mine.

00:19:09.612 --> 00:19:14.345
No one hungers
for a victory over the Jem'Hadar

00:19:14.384 --> 00:19:18.582
more than I do... no one...

00:19:18.621 --> 00:19:20.919
but we must be cautious.

00:19:20.957 --> 00:19:23.585
We cannot risk
taking this crew into combat

00:19:23.626 --> 00:19:24.923
before they're ready.

00:19:24.994 --> 00:19:26.427
They will be ready.

00:19:26.463 --> 00:19:27.930
I will see to that.

00:19:27.997 --> 00:19:29.862
I know you will, my friend.

00:19:29.899 --> 00:19:32.231
Together,
we will make the Rotarran

00:19:32.268 --> 00:19:35.931
an honorable ship again,
a ship worthy of the Empire.

00:19:35.972 --> 00:19:39.032
You may return
to your station.

00:19:45.081 --> 00:19:46.742
The Cardassians were trapped

00:19:46.783 --> 00:19:48.614
between us
and the asteroid field.

00:19:48.651 --> 00:19:49.777
It was perfect.

00:19:49.819 --> 00:19:51.047
Their power was failing.

00:19:51.087 --> 00:19:52.714
They had no other ships nearby

00:19:52.756 --> 00:19:54.747
and our weapons
were fully charged.

00:19:54.791 --> 00:19:58.158
And we were still denied
a victory.

00:19:58.194 --> 00:20:01.721
Three Jem'Hadar ships appeared
from out of the asteroid field.

00:20:01.765 --> 00:20:03.494
Three to one are long odds.

00:20:03.533 --> 00:20:05.296
I'd say you did well just...

00:20:05.335 --> 00:20:07.496
getting away
with your ship in one piece.

00:20:07.537 --> 00:20:10.665
Getting away is something
we've become very good at.

00:20:10.707 --> 00:20:12.470
The Rotarran
can run away from battle

00:20:12.509 --> 00:20:14.306
faster than any ship
in the Quadrant.

00:20:14.344 --> 00:20:16.710
You never could handle
your bloodwine, Leskit.

00:20:16.746 --> 00:20:18.976
You sound
like a sniveling Ferengi

00:20:19.048 --> 00:20:20.811
crying about lost profit.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:23.341
That's supposed
to wound my pride

00:20:23.386 --> 00:20:25.354
but Tavana has forgotten

00:20:25.388 --> 00:20:27.754
that no one serving
on the Rotarran

00:20:27.791 --> 00:20:29.258
has any pride left.

00:20:29.292 --> 00:20:31.590
Does that include me?

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.527
I do not wish to insult someone
who brought me wine

00:20:37.567 --> 00:20:39.933
but one does wonder

00:20:39.969 --> 00:20:42.904
why the successor
to the great Curzon Dax

00:20:42.939 --> 00:20:46.204
would consent to serve
upon a ship like this.

00:20:46.242 --> 00:20:47.800
It's no mystery.

00:20:47.844 --> 00:20:50.244
She's the parmach'kai
of our new First Officer.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:54.307
I heard it on the space station
before we left.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:57.183
Worf is only part
of the reason I'm here.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:21:01.020
I think it is an honor
to serve under General Martok.

00:21:01.057 --> 00:21:02.752
You mean the one-eyed giant?

00:21:03.827 --> 00:21:06.387
I wouldn't let him
hear you say that.

00:21:06.429 --> 00:21:07.828
He won't.

00:21:07.864 --> 00:21:10.492
Unless Worf is not the only one

00:21:10.533 --> 00:21:13.127
you're sharing a bed with
this trip.

00:21:13.169 --> 00:21:14.932
On this trip

00:21:14.971 --> 00:21:17.337
my bed is as empty as yours,
Leskit

00:21:17.373 --> 00:21:21.104
except mine is empty by choice.

00:21:22.812 --> 00:21:25.406
Now, that is a sound
I haven't heard

00:21:25.448 --> 00:21:27.541
on this ship for a long time.

00:21:27.584 --> 00:21:29.484
It won't last.

00:21:29.519 --> 00:21:34.422
This ship is made for tears,
not laughter.

00:21:34.457 --> 00:21:37.449
You're really not much fun
at parties, are you, Kornan?

00:21:37.494 --> 00:21:39.291
Make your jokes.

00:21:39.329 --> 00:21:43.265
Hold off fate for another day
if you can

00:21:43.299 --> 00:21:48.760
but this ship and all the souls
within its hull are cursed.

00:21:48.805 --> 00:21:51.000
Death and dishonor

00:21:51.107 --> 00:21:53.575
walk these corridors
like members of the crew.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:55.510
Aw, you talk too much, Kornan.

00:21:55.545 --> 00:21:57.410
Tell me you
don't believe it, too.

00:21:59.649 --> 00:22:01.276
We've cloaked.

00:22:01.317 --> 00:22:03.410
Alert Status One.

00:22:03.453 --> 00:22:05.421
A Jem'Hadar patrol ship
is directly ahead.

00:22:05.455 --> 00:22:07.423
Prepare for combat operations.

00:22:10.994 --> 00:22:12.689
Now you will see.

00:22:12.729 --> 00:22:17.189
Either death or dishonor
will visit us this day

00:22:17.233 --> 00:22:20.862
and there will be nothing
that you or I

00:22:20.904 --> 00:22:23.372
or any of us can do about it.

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:35.618
What are they doing here

00:22:35.652 --> 00:22:37.984
this far
from the Cardassian border?

00:22:38.054 --> 00:22:39.112
They're conducting

00:22:39.155 --> 00:22:40.884
active polaron scans
of this sector.

00:22:40.924 --> 00:22:43.722
It's likely they're on some kind
of reconnaissance mission.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:46.194
Can their scans penetrate
our cloak?

00:22:46.229 --> 00:22:47.196
I'd say there's less

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:48.993
than a three percent
chance of detection.

00:22:49.098 --> 00:22:50.565
What's our weapons status?

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:52.500
Torpedo bays are loaded.
Warheads are armed.

00:22:52.535 --> 00:22:55.003
Disruptors are locked on target.

00:22:55.104 --> 00:22:55.934
They've increased speed.

00:22:55.972 --> 00:22:57.462
They're beginning to pull away.

00:22:57.507 --> 00:22:58.667
Shall I match velocity?

00:22:59.976 --> 00:23:01.102
No.

00:23:01.144 --> 00:23:03.806
Take us back
to our original course.

00:23:03.846 --> 00:23:07.509
Forgive this unworthy officer's
poor hearing

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:09.347
but what was your order?

00:23:09.385 --> 00:23:11.819
Take us back
to our original course!

00:23:11.854 --> 00:23:15.449
Our priority
is to find the B'Moth.

00:23:20.997 --> 00:23:22.794
Sir, we have them in our sights.

00:23:22.832 --> 00:23:23.799
They cannot escape if...

00:23:23.833 --> 00:23:24.822
No, Worf.

00:23:24.867 --> 00:23:26.164
But letting the ship go...

00:23:26.202 --> 00:23:27.794
Do not question me!

00:23:29.339 --> 00:23:30.966
Is the course laid in?

00:23:31.007 --> 00:23:32.235
Yes, Captain.

00:23:32.275 --> 00:23:34.766
I await your next command.

00:23:34.811 --> 00:23:37.803
Engage.

00:23:45.989 --> 00:23:48.457
Stand down from Alert Status.

00:23:48.491 --> 00:23:50.322
You have the Bridge.

00:23:55.698 --> 00:23:57.029
Commander.

00:24:01.104 --> 00:24:02.604
That was a mistake.

00:24:02.737 --> 00:24:04.227
We shouldn't have let them go.

00:24:04.272 --> 00:24:08.504
Our orders are to find
the B'Moth, not seek combat.

00:24:08.543 --> 00:24:10.511
It was a prudent decision.

00:24:10.545 --> 00:24:12.240
To hell with prudence.

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:13.941
This isn't
a Federation starship.

00:24:14.048 --> 00:24:15.879
This is a Klingon bird-of-prey.

00:24:15.917 --> 00:24:17.782
We could've had an easy victory

00:24:17.819 --> 00:24:21.152
and in case you haven't noticed,
this crew could use a victory.

00:24:21.189 --> 00:24:22.622
Enough.

00:24:22.657 --> 00:24:23.624
You may be my parmach'kai

00:24:23.658 --> 00:24:25.057
but that does not
give you the right...

00:24:25.093 --> 00:24:27.755
I'm an officer on this ship

00:24:27.795 --> 00:24:29.660
and I am trying
to warn my superior

00:24:29.697 --> 00:24:32.165
that a dangerous situation
is developing

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:34.760
and that he'd better
do something about it.

00:24:34.802 --> 00:24:37.327
What do you mean "dangerous"?

00:24:39.407 --> 00:24:42.171
Take a good look
around you, Commander.

00:24:42.210 --> 00:24:44.770
Maybe it's just me

00:24:44.812 --> 00:24:46.302
but I think we're in trouble.

00:24:58.393 --> 00:25:00.190
I brought you here to support me

00:25:00.228 --> 00:25:02.253
not to undermine my authority.

00:25:02.296 --> 00:25:05.390
I am simply trying to point out
that we had an opportunity

00:25:05.433 --> 00:25:08.925
to destroy an enemy ship
with little risk to ourselves.

00:25:08.970 --> 00:25:10.631
Little risk?

00:25:12.306 --> 00:25:14.934
What if they'd have gotten off
a distress call

00:25:14.976 --> 00:25:16.671
before we could destroy them?

00:25:16.711 --> 00:25:18.178
They could have given away
our position

00:25:18.212 --> 00:25:19.179
called in reinforcements.

00:25:19.213 --> 00:25:20.942
We would have spent
the next three days

00:25:21.049 --> 00:25:22.209
avoiding Jem'Hadar ships

00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:24.616
instead of carrying
out our mission.

00:25:24.652 --> 00:25:27.382
No, my friend.

00:25:27.422 --> 00:25:29.788
No...

00:25:29.824 --> 00:25:32.793
This was not the right time
for battle.

00:25:36.097 --> 00:25:40.227
You question my judgment
in this matter?

00:25:41.235 --> 00:25:42.793
No.

00:25:42.837 --> 00:25:43.963
Good.

00:25:44.038 --> 00:25:47.405
Without your support,
I cannot command this ship.

00:25:49.077 --> 00:25:51.102
Tell me...

00:25:51.145 --> 00:25:53.978
that I have not made a mistake

00:25:54.015 --> 00:25:55.880
in making you my First Officer.

00:25:55.917 --> 00:25:58.044
You have my full support,
General.

00:26:00.254 --> 00:26:02.916
I knew you would not fail me,
Worf

00:26:02.957 --> 00:26:07.417
and you can rest assured,
I will not fail you.

00:26:18.439 --> 00:26:22.136
Two years, I spent
on the Cardassian border.

00:26:22.176 --> 00:26:25.942
Two years fighting Guls
and Legates and Glinns.

00:26:26.013 --> 00:26:28.345
They were cunning enemies.

00:26:28.382 --> 00:26:30.077
Always had us chasing

00:26:30.118 --> 00:26:33.053
holo-projections
and sensor ghosts.

00:26:33.087 --> 00:26:35.954
Everything was a game with them.

00:26:35.990 --> 00:26:39.687
Always had a plan
within a plan within a plan

00:26:39.727 --> 00:26:41.854
leading to a trap.

00:26:41.896 --> 00:26:44.057
It was an honor to kill them.

00:26:45.433 --> 00:26:47.731
The Cardassians.

00:26:47.769 --> 00:26:48.963
Ah!

00:26:49.003 --> 00:26:52.166
But you can respect a Cardassian

00:26:52.206 --> 00:26:56.199
because he fights for his people

00:26:56.244 --> 00:27:00.237
and he follows a code
just like we do

00:27:00.281 --> 00:27:04.274
but not the soldiers
of the Dominion

00:27:04.318 --> 00:27:06.809
not the Jem'Hadar.

00:27:06.854 --> 00:27:10.346
No. They don't fight
for anything.

00:27:10.391 --> 00:27:13.918
They fight because they're
designed that way

00:27:14.028 --> 00:27:16.826
because they're programmed
to fight.

00:27:16.864 --> 00:27:20.425
They have no honor.

00:27:20.468 --> 00:27:21.765
You're right.

00:27:21.803 --> 00:27:24.829
That's why they're
better than us.

00:27:24.872 --> 00:27:25.930
That's enough.

00:27:25.973 --> 00:27:27.941
You're on duty in an hour,
and you...

00:27:27.975 --> 00:27:30.273
Ah, the Trill doesn't want you
to know the truth

00:27:30.311 --> 00:27:32.245
my young friend

00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:36.717
but you deserve to know...
the Jem'Hadar are smarter

00:27:36.751 --> 00:27:39.242
they're faster

00:27:39.287 --> 00:27:40.879
and they're stronger
than we are.

00:27:40.922 --> 00:27:42.947
How can you say these things?!

00:27:43.057 --> 00:27:43.955
He's drunk.

00:27:44.058 --> 00:27:44.956
Ignore him.

00:27:45.059 --> 00:27:47.118
No! You listen!

00:27:47.161 --> 00:27:49.595
Listen
and maybe learn something!

00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:53.293
The Jem'Hadar are the future!

00:27:53.334 --> 00:27:54.733
Shut up, Leskit.

00:27:54.769 --> 00:27:56.669
You know why?

00:27:56.704 --> 00:27:59.537
Because they can break us.

00:27:59.574 --> 00:28:03.066
Just like they broke Martok.

00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:04.236
That's enough!

00:28:04.278 --> 00:28:06.542
She doesn't want you
to know the truth.

00:28:06.581 --> 00:28:09.550
Martok fears them.

00:28:09.584 --> 00:28:13.384
That's why
we didn't attack them.

00:28:13.421 --> 00:28:15.286
Martok fears them!

00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:41.573
Dax. Dax?

00:28:41.616 --> 00:28:42.913
What happened?

00:28:42.950 --> 00:28:44.247
Are you all right?

00:28:44.285 --> 00:28:45.912
I had to take Ortakin
to surgery.

00:28:45.953 --> 00:28:47.420
Kornan almost killed him.

00:28:47.455 --> 00:28:48.752
Why?

00:28:48.789 --> 00:28:50.154
Because Leskit was drunk.

00:28:50.191 --> 00:28:51.351
I do not understand.

00:28:51.392 --> 00:28:52.518
No, you don't understand

00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:54.255
because you're
too busy worrying

00:28:54.295 --> 00:28:56.820
about Martok
while the crew is falling apart.

00:28:59.066 --> 00:29:02.695
Kornan needed to attack someone
and he lost control

00:29:02.737 --> 00:29:04.898
but this is only the beginning.

00:29:05.006 --> 00:29:07.873
This crew has lost half
a dozen separate actions

00:29:07.909 --> 00:29:09.035
to the Jem'Hadar.

00:29:09.076 --> 00:29:11.544
The casualty list
is as long as my arm

00:29:11.579 --> 00:29:13.706
and now they're
serving under a man

00:29:13.748 --> 00:29:15.875
who seems to have
left more behind

00:29:15.917 --> 00:29:17.782
than just an eye
in that prison camp.

00:29:17.818 --> 00:29:19.615
Do not speak of the Captain
in that manner.

00:29:19.654 --> 00:29:20.882
Not while I am First Officer.

00:29:20.922 --> 00:29:24.688
Look, I like Martok

00:29:24.725 --> 00:29:27.193
but this crew needs a leader

00:29:27.228 --> 00:29:29.560
someone who'll remind
them of their duty

00:29:29.597 --> 00:29:31.360
as soldiers of the Empire

00:29:31.399 --> 00:29:34.425
and they need that leader
right now

00:29:34.468 --> 00:29:36.368
or I promise you,
they will explode.

00:29:36.404 --> 00:29:38.395
It will not come to that!

00:29:40.141 --> 00:29:42.302
I know Martok.

00:29:42.343 --> 00:29:44.402
He is a great man.

00:29:44.445 --> 00:29:47.744
He will not fail us,
but we must give him time.

00:29:47.782 --> 00:29:50.546
Time may be the one thing
we don't have, Worf.

00:29:50.584 --> 00:29:54.281
What happened in that mess hall
could happen all over this ship

00:29:54.322 --> 00:29:57.849
and if you think the blood
looks bad on my uniform

00:29:57.892 --> 00:30:01.726
wait until the decks
are dripping with it.

00:30:14.542 --> 00:30:17.170
Commander, I'm picking up
a Klingon distress call.

00:30:17.211 --> 00:30:19.679
It's very faint,
but I might be able to...

00:30:19.714 --> 00:30:21.272
It's the B'Moth.

00:30:22.650 --> 00:30:24.811
They were attacked...

00:30:24.852 --> 00:30:26.945
by the Jem'Hadar
and lost main power.

00:30:26.988 --> 00:30:29.354
Heavy casualties.

00:30:29.390 --> 00:30:31.187
At least 30 survivors.

00:30:31.225 --> 00:30:32.817
In need of assistance.

00:30:32.860 --> 00:30:34.225
Emergency power's failing.

00:30:34.261 --> 00:30:35.319
The message repeats.

00:30:35.363 --> 00:30:36.887
Location?

00:30:36.931 --> 00:30:40.833
The signal is coming
from 055 mark 342.

00:30:40.868 --> 00:30:41.994
Distance...

00:30:42.036 --> 00:30:43.799
at least seven light years.

00:30:43.838 --> 00:30:47.774
Helm, alter course
to 055 mark 342.

00:30:47.808 --> 00:30:49.742
Understood.

00:30:49.777 --> 00:30:51.335
I will inform the General.

00:30:51.379 --> 00:30:53.244
Engineer, you have the Bridge.

00:31:03.424 --> 00:31:05.892
I want to thank you
for what you did

00:31:05.926 --> 00:31:07.393
in the mess hall.

00:31:07.428 --> 00:31:09.419
Is Ortakin your parmach'kai?

00:31:11.432 --> 00:31:14.458
Things are coming
to a head on this ship.

00:31:14.502 --> 00:31:17.733
When the fighting breaks
out, stay with me.

00:31:17.772 --> 00:31:19.569
I'll protect you.

00:31:19.607 --> 00:31:23.008
I was still hoping there wasn't
going to be any fighting.

00:31:35.623 --> 00:31:36.954
Station.

00:31:40.895 --> 00:31:41.884
Station!

00:31:57.211 --> 00:31:59.372
Something is wrong here, Worf.

00:31:59.413 --> 00:32:00.880
I can feel it.

00:32:00.915 --> 00:32:03.179
If the B'Moth was attacked
by the Jem'Hadar

00:32:03.217 --> 00:32:04.946
why would there be survivors?

00:32:04.985 --> 00:32:07.317
Since we do not know
any details of the battles

00:32:07.354 --> 00:32:09.122
it is difficult to speculate.

00:32:09.255 --> 00:32:12.315
We both know the Jem'Hadar do
not leave a task half-finished.

00:32:12.358 --> 00:32:15.589
If they left the ship intact
and part of the crew still alive

00:32:15.628 --> 00:32:17.186
they did it for a reason.

00:32:17.230 --> 00:32:18.891
There could be
many explanations.

00:32:18.931 --> 00:32:21.126
The B'Moth could have
inflicted heavy damage

00:32:21.167 --> 00:32:23.658
on the Jem'Hadar ships,
forcing them to withdraw.

00:32:23.703 --> 00:32:25.295
The Jem'Hadar could
have been recalled...

00:32:25.338 --> 00:32:27.499
How is it
that I have only one eye

00:32:27.540 --> 00:32:30.407
but I can see more clearly
than anyone around me?

00:32:30.443 --> 00:32:33.173
They deliberately left survivors
on that ship.

00:32:33.212 --> 00:32:34.679
Why?

00:32:34.714 --> 00:32:37.740
Because they want someone
to try to rescue them.

00:32:37.783 --> 00:32:41.742
Oh, do not take this personally,
my friend.

00:32:41.787 --> 00:32:43.778
I spent two years
with the Jem'Hadar.

00:32:43.823 --> 00:32:47.759
I do not expect you to have
the same insight into them

00:32:47.793 --> 00:32:50.523
that I do.

00:32:50.563 --> 00:32:53.862
They're soulless creatures,
Worf.

00:32:53.900 --> 00:32:59.270
Fighting for no goal, no purpose
except to serve the Founders.

00:32:59.305 --> 00:33:01.933
They take no pleasure
in what they do.

00:33:02.008 --> 00:33:04.875
Nothing is glorified,
nothing affirmed.

00:33:04.911 --> 00:33:06.538
To the Jem'Hadar

00:33:06.579 --> 00:33:09.480
we are nothing more than...
than targets to be destroyed.

00:33:09.515 --> 00:33:11.915
I must not let them
destroy us, Worf...

00:33:11.951 --> 00:33:13.816
With all due respect, General

00:33:13.853 --> 00:33:17.755
we do not know the tactical
situation of the B'Moth yet.

00:33:17.790 --> 00:33:21.726
We should guard against making
any premature judgments.

00:33:23.596 --> 00:33:25.257
Of course.

00:33:36.609 --> 00:33:38.099
Dismissed.

00:33:49.922 --> 00:33:51.480
Rotarran Combat Log

00:33:51.524 --> 00:33:55.255
the 53rd day in the year
of Kahless 999.

00:33:55.294 --> 00:33:57.125
We have reached
the Cardassian border

00:33:57.163 --> 00:34:00.291
and begun our search
for the B'Moth.

00:34:00.333 --> 00:34:03.097
Helm... keep us at least

00:34:03.135 --> 00:34:05.626
five million kellicams
from the border.

00:34:05.671 --> 00:34:06.933
Understood.

00:34:07.039 --> 00:34:08.631
I think I've got something.

00:34:08.674 --> 00:34:10.767
It's hard to make out
through all the interference

00:34:10.810 --> 00:34:12.744
but the thermal signature
looks like a ship.

00:34:12.778 --> 00:34:15.110
It's bearing direct
to starboard

00:34:15.147 --> 00:34:17.741
at an elevation of 25 degrees.

00:34:17.783 --> 00:34:19.273
It's coming into visual range.

00:34:19.318 --> 00:34:21.047
On screen.

00:34:31.130 --> 00:34:32.927
The B'Moth.

00:34:32.965 --> 00:34:34.227
Confirmed.

00:34:34.267 --> 00:34:36.758
Helm, lay in a course
to bring us alongside.

00:34:36.802 --> 00:34:39.498
Bridge to Medical Ward.
Prepare to receive casualties.

00:34:39.538 --> 00:34:41.438
Assemble an armed boarding party
in Transporter Room 1.

00:34:41.474 --> 00:34:43.965
Make a complete search
of all the habitable areas...

00:34:44.043 --> 00:34:45.169
Hold.

00:34:45.211 --> 00:34:46.678
Commander Dax

00:34:46.712 --> 00:34:49.078
what side of the border
are they on?

00:34:49.115 --> 00:34:52.983
They're 500,000 kellicams inside
Cardassian territory, sir.

00:34:53.085 --> 00:34:55.781
They must have drifted across
a couple of days ago.

00:34:55.821 --> 00:34:59.723
There are probably
five Jem'Hadar warships

00:34:59.759 --> 00:35:01.556
out there right now

00:35:01.594 --> 00:35:04.085
just waiting for us
to cross the border.

00:35:04.130 --> 00:35:07.099
General, if they are nearby

00:35:07.133 --> 00:35:09.727
they do not care what side
of the border we are on.

00:35:09.769 --> 00:35:11.168
They will simply attack.

00:35:11.203 --> 00:35:13.194
I have explicit orders
from the High Council

00:35:13.239 --> 00:35:14.934
not to enter
Cardassian territory.

00:35:14.974 --> 00:35:16.339
I am certain the High Council

00:35:16.375 --> 00:35:18.366
will not object
under these circumstances.

00:35:18.411 --> 00:35:20.140
There are still survivors
aboard the B'Moth.

00:35:20.179 --> 00:35:21.771
We do not know that.

00:35:21.814 --> 00:35:24.282
All that we know is there is
an automated distress call.

00:35:24.317 --> 00:35:25.682
They could all be dead by now.

00:35:25.718 --> 00:35:27.686
And if they are not?

00:35:29.522 --> 00:35:32.650
Then there is nothing
we can do for them.

00:35:32.692 --> 00:35:37.322
General, you don't intend
to just leave them there?

00:35:37.363 --> 00:35:40.127
I will not throw away
the lives of this crew

00:35:40.166 --> 00:35:42.634
in a futile rescue attempt.

00:35:42.668 --> 00:35:43.965
They are Klingon warriors.

00:35:44.003 --> 00:35:44.970
We just cannot sit...

00:35:45.037 --> 00:35:46.527
I have made my decision!

00:35:46.572 --> 00:35:49.200
We will not cross the border!

00:35:51.844 --> 00:35:56.508
From this moment, anyone
who questions that... - Anyone...

00:35:56.549 --> 00:35:59.712
will be charged
with treasonable disobedience.

00:36:02.154 --> 00:36:04.145
Worf...

00:36:04.190 --> 00:36:06.385
you have the Bridge.

00:36:20.639 --> 00:36:21.833
Stations!

00:36:26.746 --> 00:36:28.737
Stations!

00:36:33.419 --> 00:36:35.649
We can't just leave those
men out there to die.

00:36:35.688 --> 00:36:37.178
No.

00:36:37.223 --> 00:36:38.952
So what are you going to do?

00:36:39.058 --> 00:36:40.719
The only thing I can do...

00:36:40.760 --> 00:36:43.627
challenge Martok
for command of the ship.

00:36:43.662 --> 00:36:45.653
I agree.

00:36:45.698 --> 00:36:49.099
But you realize, he may
not step aside willingly.

00:36:49.135 --> 00:36:50.830
I know.

00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:53.634
But if the General
will not step aside...

00:36:55.975 --> 00:36:58.034
I will have to kill him.

00:37:29.608 --> 00:37:32.736
Martok must die.

00:37:32.778 --> 00:37:34.746
That is not your decision.

00:37:34.780 --> 00:37:36.941
He is a coward.

00:37:37.016 --> 00:37:41.077
While he commands,
he dishonors us all.

00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:44.851
I shed no tears
for your dishonor, Leskit.

00:37:44.890 --> 00:37:49.418
Today would be a bad day to die

00:37:49.462 --> 00:37:51.089
son of Mogh.

00:37:51.130 --> 00:37:54.395
Take your Trill and go.

00:38:00.773 --> 00:38:02.365
Unlikely.

00:38:02.408 --> 00:38:07.004
I was hoping you would say
something like that.

00:38:15.287 --> 00:38:17.118
Alert Status One.

00:38:17.156 --> 00:38:19.647
All hands to battle stations.

00:38:19.692 --> 00:38:22.593
We are going to rescue
the survivors of the B'Moth.

00:38:26.832 --> 00:38:29.596
Who gave the order...?

00:38:29.635 --> 00:38:31.603
What's going on here?

00:38:31.637 --> 00:38:32.797
As First Officer

00:38:32.838 --> 00:38:35.238
I say that you are unfit
to serve as Captain.

00:38:35.274 --> 00:38:37.139
You what?

00:38:37.176 --> 00:38:39.940
You are a coward

00:38:40.012 --> 00:38:42.480
and I challenge you
for command of this ship.

00:38:42.515 --> 00:38:46.781
I never would have expected
this from you, Worf.

00:39:54.687 --> 00:40:00.284
Martok, Martok,
Martok, Martok...

00:40:02.393 --> 00:40:06.159
Tactical alert!
Tactical alert!

00:40:06.197 --> 00:40:09.894
There is a Jem'Hadar warship
bearing 180 mark 215.

00:40:09.934 --> 00:40:13.335
They will be within weapons
range in nine minutes.

00:40:14.805 --> 00:40:19.401
The Jem'Hadar will soon learn
to regret this day.

00:40:19.443 --> 00:40:21.411
Who is with me?!

00:40:21.445 --> 00:40:22.503
Tavana!

00:40:22.546 --> 00:40:26.676
Sometimes... I think
I know why I love you.

00:40:26.717 --> 00:40:28.480
Let's go to the Medical Ward.

00:40:28.519 --> 00:40:29.645
Shields and weapons ready.

00:40:29.687 --> 00:40:30.654
Wait.

00:40:30.688 --> 00:40:32.986
Intercept course laid in.

00:40:33.090 --> 00:40:34.990
Kol KeH less pooK loaD

00:40:35.059 --> 00:40:37.721
Kol pooK beH poo

00:40:37.762 --> 00:40:40.697
Yoch bow math bow je,
Shuv weee

00:40:40.731 --> 00:40:42.198
Say moach chu may ew...

00:40:42.233 --> 00:40:43.666
Mahk-cha!

00:40:43.701 --> 00:40:45.896
Mah Shoov, maH nong,
ej ma choch chew

00:40:45.936 --> 00:40:48.666
nee beH yln maHj,
